    intro: "A dictionary tells you what a word means; it doesn't always tell you how the word feels or which words it likes to sit next to. Learners who pick a synonym from a list can end up insulting someone (*stubborn* for *determined*) or sounding odd (*strong rain*). This lesson shows how to choose the right word, and how to guess a new word from its neighbors.",
